{"name":"Furious Tiger","hex":"#ea5814","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"furious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Feeling great anger; raging; violent.","Rushing with impetuosity; moving with violence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furious"},{"term":"tiger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Panthera tigris, a large predatory mammal of the cat family, indigenous to Asia.","A male tiger; as opposed to a tigress."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A final shouted phrase, accompanied by a jump or outstretched arms, at the end of a cheer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger","wikidata":"Q19939"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/1280px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu